        "node_id": "n_6_ee57be",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of checking every possible line segment formed by pairs of fruits, use a more efficient approach by considering the perpendicular bisectors of segments connecting pairs of fruits. This method helps identify potential slicing lines that could maximize the number of fruits intersected. Additionally, implement a data structure like a balanced binary search tree to keep track of the intersections efficiently, allowing for faster determination of the maximum number of fruits that can be sliced with a single swipe.",
